8a16","default":false,"description":"Automatically adding or removing nodes in a cluster"},{"id":1967496670,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTY3NDk2Njcw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/labels/Team:Distributed","name":"Team:Distributed","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Meta label for distributed team."}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2021-09-16T08:55:21Z","updated_at":"2021-10-15T05:18:11Z","closed_at":"2021-10-15T05:18:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"If disk thresholds are disabled on a cluster, storage based autoscaling will no longer trigger an up-scale since the mechanism detects an up-scale need based on shards that are not allocated or unable to be moved.\r\n\r\nI think there are 3 directions we can take:\r\n\r\n1. Accept this and document it. Perhaps improve the messaging.\r\n2. Make `cluster.routing.allocation.disk.threshold_enabled` and operator-privileged setting, avoiding that this is done inadvertently by users.\r\n3. Make autoscaling still trigger even with `cluster.routing.allocation.disk.threshold_enabled=false`.\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"henningandersen","id":33268011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjY4MDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33268011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/henningandersen","html_url":"https://github.com/henningandersen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/henningandersen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/henningandersen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/henningandersen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/henningandersen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https